.TH COFFIN 1 "October 26, 2026" "coffin" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
coffin \- inspect PE, ELF, and Mach-O executable files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coffin
.RI [ options ] " file"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B coffin
reads one executable file as data and prints a text report without executing it.
Supported formats include PE32/PE32+, ELF32/ELF64 in either byte order,
and thin or universal Mach-O files.
.PP
The default report includes file identity, MD5 and SHA-256 hashes, whole-file
entropy, and all applicable detail tables. Detail selectors may be combined
to choose tables; selectors unsupported by the input format are errors.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-headers
Show executable headers.
.TP
.B \-\-sections
Show sections, declared permission flags, and section entropy.
.TP
.B \-\-dependencies
Show ELF or Mach-O dependencies.
.TP
.B \-\-symbols
Show ELF or Mach-O symbols.
.TP
.B \-\-imports
Show PE imports, including delay-load imports.
.TP
.B \-\-exports
Show PE exports.
.TP
.B \-\-resources
Show PE resources and bounded decoded payload previews.
.TP
.B \-\-program-headers
Show ELF program headers.
.TP
.B \-\-load-commands
Show Mach-O load commands and segment ranges.
.TP
.B \-\-observations
Show structural observations about the file.
.TP
.B \-\-summary
Show a compact report with identity, counts, and observations.
Cannot be combined with detail selectors.
.TP
.B \-\-no-preview
Suppress resource payload previews in the report.
Resource parsing and validation still occur.
.TP
.BI \-\-entropy-window " BYTES"
Measure entropy in windows of the specified positive decimal byte size.
At most 4096 windows are permitted. This option may be specified once.
.TP
.BI \-\-code-page " N"
Specify the fallback code page for legacy PE resource text without an explicit
code page. N must be a positive decimal integer no greater than 4294967295.
This option may be specified once.
.TP
.BI \-\-extract-resources " NEW_DIRECTORY"
Extract PE resource payloads and an index.tsv file into a new directory.
Reconstruct supported standalone icon and cursor files as well.
The directory must not already exist. This option may be specified once.
Parsing failures occur before directory creation; an output I/O failure
may leave partial extracted files.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Show additional details and diagnostic progress.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End option processing. Exactly one input filename must follow;
use this for a filename beginning with a hyphen.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect an executable:
.PP
.nf
coffin /bin/ls
.fi
.PP
Select ELF sections and dependencies:
.PP
.nf
coffin \-\-sections \-\-dependencies ./program
.fi
.PP
Show a compact PE report:
.PP
.nf
coffin \-\-summary ./program.exe
.fi
.PP
Extract PE resources into a directory that does not exist:
.PP
.nf
coffin \-\-resources \-\-extract-resources ./resources ./program.exe
.fi
.PP
Measure entropy in 4096-byte windows:
.PP
.nf
coffin \-\-entropy-window 4096 ./program
.fi
.PP
Inspect a filename beginning with a hyphen:
.PP
.nf
coffin \-\- \-sample
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful inspection, or successful help/version output.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, unsupported or malformed input, resource-limit exhaustion,
or an input/output failure.
.SH LIMITS
Parsing and extraction have fixed resource budgets. Exceeding a budget is an
error, even when a larger file might otherwise be valid. Detail selectors
control presentation; they do not bypass parser validation.
.PP
PE resource trees permit at most 16 directory levels, counting the root as
level one, and 4096 directory reads. Ancestor cycles are rejected.
Repeated references to a shared subtree are allowed and charged on each visit.
Extraction is limited to 256 MiB including reconstructed image files.
.PP
Other limits bound metadata reads, table allocations, lookup work,
resource previews, and entropy measurements. These budgets do not impose
a whole-process time limit or a file-size limit on whole-file hashing.
.SH INTERPRETATION
Permission labels describe executable header flags, not runtime permissions.
Entropy and structural observations are descriptive and do not establish
whether a file is malicious. MD5 is provided for identification and comparison;
use SHA-256 for integrity checking rather than relying on MD5.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR file (1),
.BR readelf (1),
.BR objdump (1),
.BR sha256sum (1)
